<!--Post: 807--><!--Time: 1092796720-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 7:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jacob Allen was tied to a railroad track with bailing wire and was struck by a train July 5 2004 at about 3 am near Milan Kansas. The rumor is that BTKs last letter at the library claimed with evidence that he was responsible for this crime. It seemed to fit to me because of cruelty of this crime, so I thought could this have been a crime that has occurred already or even been written in a true crime as a fiction story that BTK fantasized about and then commited. I was floored when I found that a book had been written about a crime In Mena Ark. where two teens had been killed by being placed on a railroad tracks by drug related criminals as revenge for informing on them.I think BTK fantisizes about his crimes and then is highly organized in his detail in the commitment of his crimes. He is also attracted to crimes with alot of flair or unusual cruelty. Jacob Allen was a young man an athelete, what cunning it would take to get him controled by a man who is at least 50. What a challenge, Gacy was very good at doing this by using drugs alcohol and handcuffs or sex as bait. I picture BTK living in rural area south of Wichita like the tooth fairy in red dragaon in an area where no one is too close. Most of his murders were south or east of wichata there are also a rash of unsolved murders southwest of Wichita. One more note this area overlaps several different juristrictions of police which I beleive could only help you get away with murder <!--/Text--></td></tr>
