<!--Post: 812--><!--Time: 1092799382-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST812"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 8:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting that it occurred on July 5th.  Z shot Darlene Ferrin and Mike Mageau around midnight, either just prior on July 4th or just after on July 5th; Darlene was DOA at the hospital at 12:38 AM 7-5-1969. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 812-->
<!--Post: 815--><!--Time: 1092807158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST815"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 10:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If this is BTK, it&#39;s interesting that he killed a man. Latet homosexual? Otero and Bright had significant latent homosexual aspects, especially Otero. <BR> <BR>Please don&#39;t take this the wrong way but Shirley Vian was a little, well, mannish, too. And is another indication of latent homosexuality. <BR> <BR>As to BTK in his 50s &#40;I agree, Superbike7, with that age estimate&#41; and a much younger who was quite athletic and would presumably be able to fend off an attacker. &#40;Unless the attacker had a firearm and knew to stand about six or eight feet from the victims, so as not to lose control of the gun.&#41; Anyway, the age difference. &#40;Begin Douglas-O-of-Ted fame parody&#41;: <BR> <BR>We musn&#39;t overlook the element of surprise. We musn&#39;t jump to conclusions; just because it looks like a sperm overshooting an ovary does not mean it is either sperm or ovary. Ted wrote manically but brilliantly, yet reseved his most stultifying prose for public occasions. We musn&#39;t be fooled by appearances.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 815-->
<!--Post: 819--><!--Time: 1092932121-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 9:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t overlook stun gun usage. It might be impossible to detect stungun markings on a body destroyed by a train. Current stun guns run as high as 625,000&#43; volts. It is also possible to buy veterinary drugs in ag supply stores, including tranquilizing drugs, some which have a paralytic effect. Those may or may not show on a tox screen, depending on what substances are being searched. If, with blinders on, they searched for cocaine, THC, meth, Xanax, etc., it is possible to overlook some others. One of the first &#34;Unsolved Mystery&#34; Cases was just that. It took 3 exhumations before they identified the veterinary substance that produced paralysis but kept the victim perfectly conscious. <BR> <BR>With such a fresh, local kill, BTK may do cemetery visiting as well. Surely he watches the Cold Cases on A&amp;E, etc. We may soon, if we haven&#39;t already, see him copycat some of those.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 819-->
<!--Post: 1115--><!--Time: 1097190892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 07, 2004 - 4:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read today that his death was ruled a suicide. He staged it to look like a homicide. I find that strange indeed unless there was insurance monies involved that would not pay in case of a suicide. Or perhaps he tried to save face for his family.  <BR> <BR>I live in the county where the &#39;Passion of the Christ&#39; murder confession took place. That was initially ruled a suicide as well. We can only wait and see.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1115-->
<!--Post: 1444--><!--Time: 1101319150-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1444"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 24, 2004 - 9:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is an article on the net saying that the local citizenry of Argonia do not buy the suicide ruling. An article in which the train crew were interviewed stated that he was naked. Of course, his clothing could have been stipped off as a result of the impact. That is not unusual in hit and run incidents. <BR> <BR>Perhaps the police are trying subterfuge and disinformation to avert panic and increase overconfidence in a possible killer. This also reduces vigilance on the part of others as they think that they have no reason to be guarded and watchful. Sad anyway you look at it.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1444-->
<!--Post: 6616--><!--Time: 1107909442-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6616"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 4:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found an article today from CNN and from the Kansas City Channel.com. It stated that after a July 4th drinking party with his friends, Jake was passed out. His friends removed his clothing, tied him to the track with baling wire, and left him to wake up, wondering what the hell he was doing there naked. It did not work out the way they had planned. There is the tax dollar at work in education, the disintegration of the family, and a very bad joke gone very wrong. This is probably the reason they have been so closed lipped about the investigation. <BR> <BR>I wonder if they will prosecute the young men as that is at the least reckless homicide.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6616-->
<!--Post: 6677--><!--Time: 1107957771-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6677"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 6:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Something very fishy here!!! I don&#39;t believe this young man committed suicide. <BR> <BR>07/22/2004 Archived Entry: &#34;JACOB &#34;JAKE&#34; ALLEN, ARGONIA TEENAGER&#34;  <BR> <BR>They still aren&#39;t talking about the death of Jake Allen and the sheriff isn&#39;t ruling out any possibilities. Suspicious circumstances surround the death of the teenager who was tied with bailing wire to the railroad tracks near his home town of Argonia. Allen&#39;s nude body was found early July 5th along the Burlington Northern Santa Fe Corp. tracks a few miles east of Argonia. His black sweat shirt and red sweat pants were found further down the line. <BR> <BR>Allen graduated as Argonia High School&#39;s valedictorian in May. He was a member of the National Honor Society and participated in football, basketball and track. He planned to attend Northeastern Oklahoma State University. It was said he had his whole life planned out. <BR> <BR>He stayed home with his family the evening of July 4th to shoot fireworks, declining an invitation to join friends at Anthony Lake. He wasn&#39;t the kind to leave home in the middle of the night and planned to call a friend early the next morning. <BR> <BR>The investigation is being assisted by the KBI.  <BR> <BR>07/23/2004 Archived Entry: &#34;JACOB &#34;JAKE&#34; ALLEN, ARGONIA TEENAGER&#34;  <BR> <BR>The TV news report quoted the sheriff as saying &#60;b&#62;the teenager was fully clothed at the time of his death and that drugs and alcohol were not involved.&#60;b&#62;  <BR> <BR>08/23/2004 Archived Entry: &#34;JAKE ALLEN&#34;  <BR> <BR>The investigators are making headway in the Jake Allen case but they will not release any information until they are finished with their work. They are detailing all the events Allen engaged in prior to his death. They just aren&#39;t saying anything.  <BR> <BR> <BR>09/24/2004 Archived Entry: &#34;JAKE ALLEN TRAIN DEATH STILL UNDER INVESTIGATION&#34;  <BR> <BR>Wellington - - More than two months after an Argonia teenager was hit by a train, the Sumner County Sheriff&#39;s Office said Wednesday it is &#34;actively pursuing&#34; its investigation. The July 5 death of Jacob &#34;Jake&#34; Allen, has haunted this rural Kansas community since media reports surfaced that the 19-year old had apparently been tied with baling wire to the tracks.  <BR> <BR>Sumner County Sheriff Gerald Gilkey has refused to release details of the incident. <BR> <BR>In a statement Wednesday, the department said it has done 104 interviews, executed two search warrants and followed up on 49 tips. It said it also conducted four polygraphs on people rumored to be suspects in the case. <BR> <BR>&#34;Findings of those polygraphs and the investigation into these subjects have given no indication that they were involved with this incident,&#34; the department said. <BR> <BR>10/07/2004 Archived Entry: &#34;JAKE ALLEN&#39;S DEATH IS RULED A SUICIDE&#34;  <BR> <BR>The sheriff said Allen&#39;s death was a suicide staged to look like a homicide. Allen allegedly used bailing wire to tie himself to railroad tracks and was subsequently run over by a train. It was a very complete investigation by nine separate agencies and with the complete cooperation of family and friends. There was no evidence that any one else was involved in Allen&#39;s actions. <BR> <BR>Family, friends and people in Argonia are not convinced of the findings. Allen was valedictorian of his high school graduating class and had enrolled in college. He had his future staked out and planned to proceed with his plans. He came from a very loving family. It was a tragic, senseless death. By all accounts he was a good kid, outstanding student leader and had a promising future.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6677-->
<!--Post: 8462--><!--Time: 1109150730-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 1:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read a post about a guy who said he knew BTK and he had said he grew up as a youth in Anthony.This is very close to Jacob Allens death spot.His friends had invited him to Anthony lake just outside Anthony.Also their are at least four railroads that intersect this area if BTK is telling the truth this would be a likely place for him to have grown up. The story I read seemed like it could be true.One more thing this whole story about Jacob commiting suicide just doesnt make much sense or that his friends tied him to the track. I have never heard of anyone commiting suicide in such a weird way.They sure have been tight lipped with the facts about this whole story.It may not have been BTK but if it was,it would tie into his fasination with trains and be a real twist in his story.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8462-->
<!--Post: 8473--><!--Time: 1109168763-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8473"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 6:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can believe that his friends tied him to the tracks for a joke. I do not believe that he committed suicide. They should have been able to determine blood alcohol levels at least 2-3 hours prior to death by sampling the vitreous humor of the eye. No autopsy report info leaves everybody in the dark. They may think that it is none of our business. <BR> <BR>You would be amazed at the ways that people take their lives: cutting their throats with a saw or barbed wired, stabbing themselves to death, a stick of dynamite in the mouth. Such self loathing is heartbreaking. <BR> <BR><a href="http://uselesswordz.tripod.com/id29.html" target=_top>http://uselesswordz.tripod.com/id29.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8473-->
<!--Post: 8485--><!--Time: 1109174791-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George?  <BR> <BR>Otero and Bright had latent homosexual tendencies? <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t see it. <BR> <BR>It has been reported somewhere that Otero was having an affair, or mistress-type relationship, with a younger woman. The woman was questioned but she was ruled out of involvement. <BR> <BR>Other than that I haven&#39;t heard of any other love interests in Joe Otero&#39;s life before his murder. If there was one, we would know it. <BR> <BR>Teardrop... <BR> <BR>Were stun-guns sold in the 1970s?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
